        "original_id": "08b0c714-f3d5-592d-8581-2e5dbdd39207",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: 3 Arts Entertainment, Netflix, NBC\n- People: Erwin Stoff, Tina Fey, Robert Carlock, Ellie Kemper\n- Products: Down the Shore, Parks and Recreation, The Mindy Project, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia, Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt, Edge of Tomorrow, Unbroken\n- Places: Beverly Hills\n\nFacts:\n- In 1991, Erwin Stoff founded 3 Arts Entertainment in Beverly Hills to prepare for producing the television show Down the Shore.\n- 3 Arts Entertainment is a talent management and television and film production company.\n- 3 Arts Entertainment is known for producing the comedy television shows Parks and Recreation, The Mindy Project, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia, and Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt.\n- 3 Arts Entertainment is also known for producing the films Edge of Tomorrow and Unbroken.\n- Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt is an American television sitcom created by Tina Fey and Robert Carlock and starring Ellie Kemper in the title role.\n- Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt was originally planned as a 13-episode first season on NBC for spring 2015 before Netflix bought the show and ordered two seasons.\n- Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt has streamed on Netflix since March 6, 2015.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "acd74631-fb0f-5a42-b4ac-b2402fdb3838",
        "text": "Page: 3 Arts Entertainment. Sentence: 3 Arts Entertainment is a Beverly Hills–based talent management and television/film production company founded by Erwin Stoff in 1991 in preparation for producing the television show \"Down the Shore\".\nPage: 3 Arts Entertainment. Sentence: The company is best known for producing comedic TV shows \"Parks and Recreation\", \"The Mindy Project\", \"Brooklyn Nine-Nine\", \"It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia\", \"Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt\" but also for blockbuster and dramatic films \"Edge of Tomorrow\", \"Unbroken\" and \"\".\nPage: Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt. Sentence: Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt is an American television sitcom created by Tina Fey and Robert Carlock, starring Ellie Kemper in the title role, that has streamed on Netflix since March 6, 2015.\nPage: Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt. Sentence: Originally set for a 13-episode first season on NBC for spring 2015, the show was sold to Netflix and given a two-season order.",
